- entry .pick   `xs.pick(index) { i => … }`: checks an index and runs a lambda with it confined, or gives `Unset`
-     The fused form of `confine` and `let`: the lambda receives the index typed `Operand in
-     xs.type`, so its reads of `xs` are bare, and the result is `Optional`, `Unset` when the
-     index is not defined. Re-declared in the umbrella with the rest of the deindexing group.
+ entry .pick   `xs.pick(index) { i => … }`: prüft einen Index und führt ein Lambda mit ihm beschränkt aus, oder ergibt `Unset`
+     Die verschmolzene Form von `confine` und `let`: Das Lambda erhält den Index typisiert als
+     `Operand in xs.type`, sodass seine Lesezugriffe auf `xs` bloß sind, und das Ergebnis ist `Optional`,
+     `Unset`, wenn der Index nicht definiert ist. Mit dem Rest der deindizierenden Gruppe im
+     Umbrella neu deklariert.

=     index is not defined. Re-declared in the umbrella with the rest of the deindexing group.
=
-     ```scala
+     ```scala

=     index is not defined. Re-declared in the umbrella with the rest of the deindexing group.
=
=     ```scala
-     import soundness.*
+     import soundness.*

=     index is not defined. Re-declared in the umbrella with the rest of the deindexing group.
=
=     ```scala
=     import soundness.*
=
-     val xs = Sequence(10, 20, 30)
+     val xs = Sequence(10, 20, 30)

-     xs.pick(Ter) { i => xs(i) + i.n0 }   // 32
+     xs.pick(Ter) { i => xs(i) + i.n0 }   // 32

=     xs.pick(Ter) { i => xs(i) + i.n0 }   // 32
-     ```
